<http://data.silknow.org/object/0642eec7-6943-3107-af9b-1cbd69d3d88a>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Fragment of tapestry border woven in wool, silk and metal thread (either silver or silver-gilt with the gilding gone). Decorated with the top half of two putti flanking a central rod entwined with a snake just above their heads, and below the bottom of a roundel. The ground has a chequered pattern in metal thread on a yellow ground. 22-29 warp threads to the inch, 10-12 to the cm. It comes from a tapestry such as the Sujets de la Fable."@en , "Fragment of tapestry border woven in wool, silk and metal thread, made at the Gobelins, France, ca. 1670-1699"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/e2b50f9c-19c5-33f6-ad41-031c12b7f2a5> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Fragment of tapestry border woven in wool, silk and metal thread (either silver or silver-gilt with the gilding gone). Decorated with the top half of two putti flanking a central rod entwined with a snake just above their heads, and below the bottom of a roundel. The ground has a chequered pattern in metal thread on a yellow ground. 22-29 warp threads to the inch, 10-12 to the cm. It comes from a tapestry such as the Sujets de la Fable."@en , "Fragment of tapestry border woven in wool, silk and metal thread, made at the Gobelins, France, ca. 1670-1699"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/0642eec7-6943-3107-af9b-1cbd69d3d88a/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/0642eec7-6943-3107-af9b-1cbd69d3d88a/dimension/2> ;
